{"name":"Vampire Fangs","hex":"#cc2255","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vampire","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mythological creature (usually humanoid and undead) said to feed on the blood or life energy of the living. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A person with habits traditionally ascribed to (literal) vampires, such as heliophobia, being a night owl, having pale skin, and so on."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To drain of energy or resources."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vampire"},{"term":"fangs","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of fang"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of fang"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fangs"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vampire","blocks":[{"text":"A vampire is a mythical creature with a human-like appearance that subsists by feeding on the vital essence of humans. In European folklore, vampires are undead humanoid creatures that visit loved ones and cause mischief or deaths in the neighbourhoods they inhabited while they were alive. They wear shrouds and are often described as bloated and of ruddy or dark countenance, contrasting with the modern gaunt, pale vampire which dates from the early 19th century."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Philip_Burne-Jones_-_The_Vampire.jpg/330px-Philip_Burne-Jones_-_The_Vampire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire"},{"title":"Fang","blocks":[{"text":"A fang is a long, pointed tooth. In mammals, a fang is a modified maxillary tooth, used for biting and tearing flesh. In snakes, it is a specialized tooth that is associated with a venom gland. Spiders also have external fangs, which are part of the chelicerae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Fangs_01_rfc1036.jpg/330px-Fangs_01_rfc1036.jpg?utm_